WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:09.980
<b><i>We look the same, but men call us monsters. 

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:13.200
<b>Eighteen Years Earlier</b>

00:00:13.280 --> 00:00:15.200
<b>Edo Castle</b>

00:00:15.730 --> 00:00:16.990
Ninjas?

00:00:17.630 --> 00:00:20.580
Priest, you would use ninjas

00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:23.710
to decide the third Tokugawa shogun?

00:00:24.090 --> 00:00:25.370
Indeed...

00:00:25.370 --> 00:00:29.470
The struggle between the factions 
of the eldest, Takechiyo,

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:35.720
and those of the younger, Kunichiyo, 
has grown enough to be a threat.

00:00:36.130 --> 00:00:39.350
Normally, as befits a samurai family,

00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:50.980
<b>Tenkai</b>

00:00:39.350 --> 00:00:44.070
it would be possible to settle things 
with ten rounds of dueling.

00:00:44.070 --> 00:00:50.980
But it would be a shame to lose Tokugawa 
samurai over a matter like this.

00:00:57.230 --> 00:00:59.740
And thus, ninjas?

00:01:02.680 --> 00:01:04.310
If we use ninjas,

00:01:04.310 --> 00:01:08.500
even if all were to die in a sea of blood...

00:02:47.020 --> 00:02:49.430
We're on the ship now.

00:02:49.430 --> 00:02:51.000
Just accept it.

00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:53.020
I know.

00:02:55.820 --> 00:03:00.780
<b><i>Advent of Joujin</i></b>

00:03:03.280 --> 00:03:06.790
My lord, please calm yourself.

00:03:06.790 --> 00:03:08.320
I, Bunnoshin,

00:03:08.320 --> 00:03:12.170
have set a second and third 
layer of traps for him.

00:03:12.380 --> 00:03:14.540
A second and third layer?

00:03:14.540 --> 00:03:15.610
Yes, my lord.

00:03:15.610 --> 00:03:18.420
The next trap is "the ears."

00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:19.830
The ears?

00:03:20.420 --> 00:03:24.430
I have picked someone with excellent 
ears to be our archery commander.

00:03:24.680 --> 00:03:28.420
With his ears, he can locate a foe,

00:03:28.840 --> 00:03:34.690
using only footsteps and other sounds.

00:03:35.200 --> 00:03:36.400
I see.

00:03:36.400 --> 00:03:40.310
Then, they will be unaffected 
by Hachirou's eye magic.

00:03:40.890 --> 00:03:42.330
How many bowmen are there?

00:03:42.330 --> 00:03:43.800
Twenty, in all.

00:03:44.370 --> 00:03:48.120
Twenty arrows over the wall

00:03:48.120 --> 00:03:52.330
are too much for even a 
monstrous ninja to survive.

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:16.110
<i>I know that autumn can be a painful thing, 
but I shall never tire of the sound</i>

00:04:10.520 --> 00:04:16.110
<b></b>

00:04:16.560 --> 00:04:19.110
<b></b>

00:04:16.680 --> 00:04:18.730
<i>of the bell crickets.</i>

00:05:09.840 --> 00:05:10.810
<i>Shichigen...</i>

00:05:12.760 --> 00:05:14.910
The archers were wiped out?

00:05:15.320 --> 00:05:16.070
Yes, my lord.

00:05:16.070 --> 00:05:19.950
They failed to strike the wicked 
Hachirou with even a single arrow.

00:05:20.790 --> 00:05:21.800
Bunnoshin!

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.960
B-But we still have the third layer.

00:05:25.960 --> 00:05:28.100
The rifleman.

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:29.870
However...

00:05:29.870 --> 00:05:31.560
Have you forgotten?

00:05:31.560 --> 00:05:35.560
Gorouza the Hawk accompanies the rifleman.

00:05:35.830 --> 00:05:37.560
Oh, he does?

00:05:37.810 --> 00:05:38.910
Indeed, my lord.

00:05:38.910 --> 00:05:42.790
Gorouza the Hawk was the best 
student of Otowanokido,

00:05:42.790 --> 00:05:47.240
who shot Oda Nobunaga in the 
forest of Aekunimyoujin.

00:05:47.570 --> 00:05:50.070
I am told he surpasses even his master.

00:05:53.460 --> 00:05:58.080
I had the opportunity to 
see his skill, only once.

00:05:58.460 --> 00:06:01.640
He downed a rainbird, flying faster 
than the eye could see,

00:06:01.640 --> 00:06:02.900
with a single shot.

00:06:19.880 --> 00:06:22.240
I have heard those rumors.

00:06:22.240 --> 00:06:24.730
Then, Gorouza is with us?

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:29.250
It would be impossible for him to miss.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:32.370
Stay here and await good news.

00:06:32.370 --> 00:06:34.590
I shall!

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:36.780
I'm thirsty. Bring tea.

00:06:36.780 --> 00:06:39.370
No, sake! Prepare sake!

00:06:39.610 --> 00:06:41.690
Yes, my lord. Please wait a moment.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:03.360
He's far away.

00:07:03.360 --> 00:07:04.680
Aim carefully.

00:07:04.680 --> 00:07:05.450
Stop.

00:07:10.260 --> 00:07:12.410
I don't want to kill you.

00:07:12.410 --> 00:07:13.800
Are you with him?

00:07:13.800 --> 00:07:14.530
Fire!

00:07:22.160 --> 00:07:24.670
I told you I didn't want to kill you...

00:07:58.820 --> 00:08:00.080
Hachirou...

00:08:01.230 --> 00:08:02.370
Shikibu?

00:08:48.900 --> 00:08:50.250
Wind...

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:54.000
Southeast to northwest 3.

00:08:54.000 --> 00:08:55.760
Adjustment 1.5,

00:08:55.760 --> 00:08:57.140
mixed, to the west...

00:09:44.080 --> 00:09:45.580
The murderous intent is gone.

00:09:46.540 --> 00:09:47.440
We're fine.

00:10:03.930 --> 00:10:06.730
His eyes were too good, 
and cost him his life?

00:10:11.650 --> 00:10:13.960
Wait! Where are you going?

00:10:15.150 --> 00:10:18.590
Hachirou, why do you ignore us?

00:10:18.960 --> 00:10:22.600
Why do you sneak around, all by yourself?

00:10:23.030 --> 00:10:26.980
That's right. We were worried about you...

00:10:29.490 --> 00:10:30.860
Say something!

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:33.580
Shichigen. Shikibu.

00:10:34.030 --> 00:10:38.110
I will avenge the Five Treasures 
and our friends in the village.

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:40.490
That is my job.

00:10:41.040 --> 00:10:44.700
Hachirou, you're our leader.

00:10:44.700 --> 00:10:48.940
Our job is to protect you and your bloodline!

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.370
It's fine...

00:10:50.370 --> 00:10:52.070
Let him go.

00:10:53.220 --> 00:10:54.380
Saizou...

00:10:54.910 --> 00:11:00.010
Just doing what the boss
tells us to do is also our job.

00:11:22.230 --> 00:11:23.620
Utsutsu and Rui are gone?

00:11:24.050 --> 00:11:26.910
Yeah. I can't find them anywhere.

00:11:26.910 --> 00:11:28.620
It's time to open the shop soon.

00:11:32.000 --> 00:11:35.880
They must've gone to check 
out that big thing.

00:11:35.880 --> 00:11:37.270
Even Rui?

00:11:37.780 --> 00:11:41.210
I told her to stay here until 
Namenba returned...

00:11:42.270 --> 00:11:44.140
Until I what?

00:11:47.670 --> 00:11:48.940
Namenba!

00:12:10.640 --> 00:12:11.660
What are you doing?

00:12:12.630 --> 00:12:14.370
Making a drawing.

00:12:14.370 --> 00:12:19.280
Gorone might be able to learn something 
about its structure or weaknesses.

00:12:26.570 --> 00:12:27.180
Someone's coming!

00:12:31.550 --> 00:12:33.440
Just farmers.

00:12:33.440 --> 00:12:34.490
Wait.

00:12:53.740 --> 00:12:54.970
I'll take a bowl.

00:12:54.970 --> 00:12:56.210
Coming up!

00:12:59.460 --> 00:13:03.470
The soba here is quite good.

00:13:07.590 --> 00:13:09.400
Is that you, Gobo?

00:13:10.110 --> 00:13:11.600
Thanks to you,

00:13:12.890 --> 00:13:14.850
I went through quite the mess.

00:13:15.460 --> 00:13:17.100
Nonsense...

00:13:17.100 --> 00:13:19.860
Suruga-sama's forces can't be that dangerous.

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:24.290
I didn't have the slightest concern

00:13:24.290 --> 00:13:28.490
that you would easily defeat them.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.950
I failed to mention that

00:13:42.950 --> 00:13:46.310
I am High Priest Tenkai's ninja monk.

00:13:47.060 --> 00:13:52.910
I was simply getting close to 
Suruga-sama by his order.

00:13:53.450 --> 00:13:54.870
Tenkai?

00:13:58.810 --> 00:13:59.910
Here, you—

00:14:03.240 --> 00:14:04.500
Um...

00:14:10.860 --> 00:14:13.550
It looks like the rain didn't last.

00:14:13.550 --> 00:14:15.600
Thanks. It was good.

00:14:16.230 --> 00:14:17.290
You're welcome.

00:14:24.360 --> 00:14:25.630
Saizou.

00:14:25.630 --> 00:14:27.860
Why did you let Hachirou go?

00:14:27.860 --> 00:14:30.130
I can't accept it!

00:14:30.130 --> 00:14:31.300
Hey, Saizou!

00:14:31.500 --> 00:14:33.060
Are you listening?

00:14:41.760 --> 00:14:42.820
What was that for?

00:14:43.040 --> 00:14:44.080
Answer me!

00:14:44.080 --> 00:14:47.950
Didn't you help Hachirou because 
you wanted him to come back?!

00:14:49.030 --> 00:14:51.950
You and I play the game differently.

00:14:51.950 --> 00:14:54.580
You never make any damn sense!

00:14:54.580 --> 00:14:56.090
Don't fight!

00:14:57.600 --> 00:15:02.150
I think he wants no blood 
to be shed but his own.

00:15:03.650 --> 00:15:06.960
He's always cared about us, 
ever since he was a kid.

00:15:07.730 --> 00:15:13.970
Normally, a ninja leader tells 
his men to go and die for him.

00:15:14.750 --> 00:15:18.730
So two weirdos were drawn to each other, huh?

00:15:19.110 --> 00:15:21.020
Don't you think it's interesting?

00:15:21.400 --> 00:15:25.230
Weird ninjas protecting 
their weird ninja leader.

00:15:25.880 --> 00:15:28.600
You can't use an established 
playbook with that...

00:15:28.600 --> 00:15:31.990
The game won't go the way it should.

00:15:32.300 --> 00:15:35.300
You're so stubborn.

00:15:36.020 --> 00:15:39.150
Anyway, back to the tea stand.

00:15:39.150 --> 00:15:40.750
Something is bothering me.

00:15:59.070 --> 00:16:01.770
You didn't get to eat your soba noodles.

00:16:02.270 --> 00:16:06.650
Since you mentioned the name 
Tenkai, I won't talk with you.

00:16:07.440 --> 00:16:10.680
He was the one who created the 
battle between Iga and Kouga.

00:16:11.700 --> 00:16:14.310
Your mortal enemy, then?

00:16:14.310 --> 00:16:17.530
That's very narrow-minded.

00:16:18.030 --> 00:16:19.160
Narrow-minded?

00:16:19.400 --> 00:16:22.840
Who is the enemy you now face?

00:16:22.840 --> 00:16:24.940
Please think carefully.

00:16:25.450 --> 00:16:27.640
If you want to defeat that foe,

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:30.670
you have no need for long-forgotten grudges.

00:16:31.190 --> 00:16:35.390
It's all just an old story for you.

00:16:35.820 --> 00:16:40.680
So you want me to forget 
everything and help you?

00:16:41.960 --> 00:16:48.670
The Joujinshuu are our common enemy.

00:16:50.040 --> 00:16:52.560
If you can promise us your aid,

00:16:52.560 --> 00:16:54.790
we can start repaying you

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:57.900
by giving you some of Joujin's secrets.

00:16:57.900 --> 00:16:59.830
Joujin's secrets?

00:16:59.830 --> 00:17:00.790
Indeed.

00:17:01.650 --> 00:17:03.420
I'm not interested.

00:17:03.420 --> 00:17:07.430
You're intending to lie and 
use us again, aren't you?

00:17:08.150 --> 00:17:10.360
We aren't your pawns!

00:17:12.090 --> 00:17:13.170
How awful...

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.530
This is just terrible.

00:17:14.530 --> 00:17:16.790
Yes, it is brutal.

00:17:16.790 --> 00:17:19.810
But that is the destiny of the ninja.

00:17:19.810 --> 00:17:23.730
Hachirou, you will be the 
leader of these ninjas.

00:17:24.010 --> 00:17:27.350
You will need to be ready to sacrifice them,

00:17:27.350 --> 00:17:29.780
if the situation demands.

00:17:30.530 --> 00:17:32.110
I don't want to.

00:17:32.530 --> 00:17:34.110
Hachirou...

00:17:36.080 --> 00:17:37.530
I refuse!

00:17:38.340 --> 00:17:41.120
If you will not leave me alone...

00:17:47.580 --> 00:17:50.110
I thought your eye magic would be useless

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:53.880
against one who didn't consider you an enemy.

00:18:00.860 --> 00:18:03.200
Hundreds of years ago,

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:08.650
a monk traveled to Sòng, where he 
performed a prayer for rain.

00:18:11.320 --> 00:18:13.700
His name was Joujin.

00:18:13.700 --> 00:18:18.660
They say his power caused the rain to fall...

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:22.560
No, it was probably a coincidence.

00:18:23.620 --> 00:18:26.570
But isn't that somewhat eerie?

00:18:28.500 --> 00:18:30.290
It is said that Joujin

00:18:30.290 --> 00:18:34.500
has many other soldiers beyond the Five.

00:18:34.930 --> 00:18:36.940
They are called the Rain.

00:18:44.140 --> 00:18:46.060
Utsutsu, this is bad.

00:18:46.060 --> 00:18:47.860
There are more.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:49.060
Let's go back.

00:19:15.000 --> 00:19:16.750
Rui, I'll charge in.

00:19:16.750 --> 00:19:17.940
Follow me.

00:19:17.940 --> 00:19:19.220
Got it, Utsutsu!

00:19:30.100 --> 00:19:31.850
Utsutsu, wait!

00:19:32.150 --> 00:19:33.350
This way!

00:19:35.200 --> 00:19:36.510
How far are you going?

00:19:36.510 --> 00:19:37.610
Where else?

00:19:37.950 --> 00:19:39.500
To the pier with the boat.

00:19:42.630 --> 00:19:43.890
Wait, Utsutsu...

00:19:43.890 --> 00:19:45.240
Utsutsu, wait!

00:19:45.660 --> 00:19:47.230
Don't leave me.

00:19:53.450 --> 00:19:54.960
Utsutsu, where are you?

00:19:54.960 --> 00:19:56.250
Over here, Rui!

00:20:01.470 --> 00:20:02.740
Over here, Rui.

00:20:02.960 --> 00:20:04.010
Over here, Rui.

00:20:04.010 --> 00:20:05.760
The Rain has arrived.

00:21:09.280 --> 00:21:12.750
You say all the riflemen are dead?

00:21:13.020 --> 00:21:13.970
Yes, my lord!

00:21:14.730 --> 00:21:16.520
And Gorouza the Hawk?

00:21:16.520 --> 00:21:17.930
Yes, my lord!

00:21:19.930 --> 00:21:21.790
Oh, dear...

00:21:22.220 --> 00:21:23.390
Who's there?!

00:21:23.390 --> 00:21:28.060
Perhaps, now, your treason will be revealed.

00:21:28.060 --> 00:21:29.450
Damn you—

00:21:32.100 --> 00:21:35.780
Hello again, Suruga-sama.

00:21:35.780 --> 00:21:38.230
Wh-Who are you?

00:21:38.980 --> 00:21:43.030
Oh, my. Have you forgotten me?

00:21:46.570 --> 00:21:51.040
Suruga-sama, it is I.

00:21:52.380 --> 00:21:53.970
Joujin...

00:23:25.000 --> 00:23:27.010
<b><i>Preview</i></b>

00:23:25.710 --> 00:23:30.260
A failed young man, who once wanted 
to be king, finds his heart in distress.

00:23:30.260 --> 00:23:33.010
The Kouga and Iga gather once more,

00:23:33.010 --> 00:23:35.510
and head for Murakumo Castle.

00:23:35.510 --> 00:23:38.520
<b><i>The Butterfly Dances</i></b>

00:23:35.930 --> 00:23:38.520
And dance...
